 "seat": {
  "BEST_WHY": "The wall run above the room (y\u2248370\u2013455, full width) is stacked in the right order and reads as built: soft-lit top surface, then a continuous 2px dark cap line at y\u2248423, then one crisp course of face bricks with staggered joints, then floor. The corridor mouth at x\u2248505\u2013560 resolves into a coherent lit pillar whose shaft shading runs vertically and whose face course ends cleanly against it. On the floor, the joints between stones vary in width and darkness along a single course (compare the run at y\u2248540\u2013560 from x\u2248420 to x\u2248640), individual stones carry different hatch densities, and the lit patch dims stone-by-stone rather than as a flat gradient, so the floor reads as laid, not stamped. Nothing in the frame is a prop that can go wrong; the base tileset is doing all the work and it holds up.",
  "WORST_WHY": "The pool at (248\u2013343, 0\u2013192) is a hard-edged rectangle of hex-pattern green with a 1px lighter border and no bank, lip, shadow or wet edge where it meets the dirt \u2014 it reads as a placeholder region fill. The same moss decal is pasted three times on the wall tops at (13\u201347, 55\u201390), (13\u201345, 205\u2013230) and (350\u2013384, 145\u2013175), unchanged; the same lily pad is pasted four times in the pool; the two crates at (63\u201397, 0\u201340) and (63\u201397, 48\u201388) are pixel-identical, as are the two barrels at (115\u2013143, 195\u2013215) and (163\u2013191, 195\u2013215). The crates, barrels and orc are drawn 3/4-view (they show a front face and a top) while the walls and floor are strict top-down, so the objects sit on the floor at a different projection from the room. The frame is evenly lit edge to edge \u2014 no light source, no falloff, no shadow under any object. The \"bones\" at (207\u2013237, 113\u2013130) are an unreadable white pixel scatter.",
  "FLAGGED": "1, 2, 3",
